<title>USA: MainStay creates income fund.</title>
<headline>MainStay creates income fund.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>MainStay Funds said it launched the MainStay Strategic Income Fund, which will invest primarily in international and domestic fixed income securities, including investment grade, government and high-yield bonds.</p>
<p>The fund is being managed by  MacKay-Shields Financial Corp, led by Neil Feinberg, who will be responsible for asset allocation.</p>
<p>MainStay is a unit of  New York Life Insurance Co and has 14 retail funds.  Including its institutional funds, MainStay has $12.9 billion in assets uinder management.</p>
</text>
